1
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:04,130
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:14,810
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

3
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:41,440
[blows]

4
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,730
All right, that should do it.

5
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:45,520
Wow, so cool.

6
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:47,820
You make all of your weapons
and stuff yourself?

7
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:49,980
Yeah, I can pretty much
make everything

8
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:51,150
that I need to survive.

9
00:01:51,690 --> 00:01:53,780
I learned most of it
from my dad.

10
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:55,530
Figured out the rest myself.

11
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:58,200
At that point, I was on my own.

12
00:02:01,410 --> 00:02:03,750
I'd like to find someplace
I can try it out.

13
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:08,460
Yuru, do you think you could
teach me how to use a weapon?

14
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:09,800
[YURU] Mm?

15
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:12,880
[KEN] I want to get stronger.

16
00:02:12,930 --> 00:02:14,430
♪

17
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:16,090
[Ken sighs]

18
00:02:18,430 --> 00:02:19,560
[YURU] Sure.

19
00:02:19,930 --> 00:02:20,930
I can do that.

20
00:02:20,970 --> 00:02:22,020
EPISODE 12
RETAINER AND SHAMAN

21
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:23,390
[birds chirping]

22
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,230
[TACHIKAWA] Hello.

23
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:29,320
[Akai and Midori whining]

24
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,200
[GABBY AND ASA] Uh?

25
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,200
[TACHIKAWA] Hm?

26
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:41,240
Oh, hey, it's you.
Sorry, uh...

27
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:43,830
The name's Makoto.
Makoto Tachikawa.

28
00:02:43,870 --> 00:02:45,330
It's nice seeing you again.

29
00:02:45,370 --> 00:02:47,750
Of course, I remember now.

30
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:48,960
Nice to see you.

31
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,210
Great, the chick
with the woodland creatures.

32
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:53,340
[ASA] So are you working today?

33
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:56,090
[TACHIKAWA] Yep.
Jin asked me to come in.

34
00:02:57,140 --> 00:02:59,510
[ASA] And hello to you, too,
Akai and Midori.

35
00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:00,560
[Akai and Midori grunt]

36
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:03,140
By the way,
what are their abilities?

37
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:04,810
We haven't seen them
in action yet.

38
00:03:04,850 --> 00:03:07,150
They're good at kidnappings
and abductions.

39
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:08,350
That sort of thing.

40
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:11,070
Isn't that Yin-Yang's
specialty, too?

41
00:03:11,110 --> 00:03:13,360
Hiding people and then
spitting them back out again?

42
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,690
[Daifuku and Ohagi scream]

43
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:16,320
Oh, I see.

44
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:18,740
And the point of the raid
was to kidnap me and Yuru,

45
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,830
so it makes sense
you'd be recruited for it.

46
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:24,120
So how do your daemons
do their snatching, Mako?

47
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:26,790
A nickname, that's fun.

48
00:03:27,170 --> 00:03:29,710
Well, Akai can transform
into a person,

49
00:03:29,750 --> 00:03:32,420
so we use that ability
to honey trap our targets.

50
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:35,760
As for Midori,
well, they say tanuki

51
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,050
are as broad
as eight tatami mats.

52
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:42,180
They stretch out a ton,
kinda like a giant net.

53
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:45,640
Then they can instantly envelop
someone to kidnap them.

54
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,690
[ASA AND GABBY]
They use their eight-mat

55
00:03:47,730 --> 00:03:49,730
to envelop and kidnap people.

56
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:51,020
Pure evil.

57
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,230
In fact, the little guy
actually fought

58
00:03:53,270 --> 00:03:55,650
in the legendary
Shikoku tanuki war.

59
00:03:55,690 --> 00:03:57,570
[GABBY] Can you imagine
being abducted

60
00:03:57,610 --> 00:03:59,280
by a tanuki nut sack?

61
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,160
That's like nightmare fuel.

62
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:03,080
[ASA] Thank you so much
for kidnapping me

63
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,830
before Midori could, Yin-Yang.

64
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:06,210
I owe you guys.

65
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:10,460
[GABBY] Midori may be
the most terrifying daemon ever.

66
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:14,340
So, Jin, what is this work
that you summoned Tachikawa here

67
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:15,500
to take care of today?

68
00:04:15,550 --> 00:04:17,840
You wouldn't be planning
to use Midori

69
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,930
to kidnap my brother,
now would you?

70
00:04:19,970 --> 00:04:21,470
No, of course not.

71
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:24,060
She came to help us solve
the mystery

72
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:26,140
of the non-existent west gate.

73
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:29,640
Okay, weird.

74
00:04:29,690 --> 00:04:32,690
There was definitely a gate
in that wall before.

75
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,570
I remember the spot.

76
00:04:34,610 --> 00:04:36,150
Everything else is still here.

77
00:04:36,190 --> 00:04:38,150
That big rock
and the fruit trees.

78
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:40,610
Which means the gate
should be right over there.

79
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:43,370
I'm absolutely sure.
So where the heck did it go?

80
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,790
Sensei's daemons
can rewrite reality.

81
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:48,870
We would know
if it had been him, though.

82
00:04:48,910 --> 00:04:50,830
The changes he makes
always take a while

83
00:04:50,870 --> 00:04:52,420
to blend in
with their surroundings.

84
00:04:58,210 --> 00:04:59,260
[JIN] Hm.

85
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:01,050
♪

86
00:05:03,430 --> 00:05:05,720
There actually are faint lines
visible here.

87
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:06,890
[ALL] Hm?

88
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:08,980
[ASA] Where?

89
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:10,020
Wait.

90
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:12,100
I can see it.
Like a clean cut.

91
00:05:12,730 --> 00:05:13,980
[ASA] Uh?

92
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,110
And another one!

93
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:20,650
Well, folks...

94
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:23,620
Don't know about you,
but it looks like a gate to me.

95
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:27,950
It wasn't made
by a simple razor. No way.

96
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:31,120
It had to have been
much sharper.

97
00:05:32,330 --> 00:05:33,500
[beeping]

98
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:35,540
[FEMALE ASSISTANT]
Mr. Shingo, you have a guest

99
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:36,750
at the front desk.

100
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:39,050
[SHINGO] All right,
you can send him up.

101
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:43,550
[knocking on door]

102
00:05:43,590 --> 00:05:45,140
[EMPLOYEE] Your guest, sir.

103
00:05:51,890 --> 00:05:54,100
Uncle, hello!

104
00:05:54,770 --> 00:05:57,560
Hello, Asuma. You look well.

105
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,320
I am, thank you.

106
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:01,360
Sorry for always making you
come to me.

107
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:02,900
Not very considerate, huh?

108
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:04,660
If that's how you really feel,

109
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:06,200
it would be
simple enough to fix.

110
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:07,870
You could visit the manor

111
00:06:07,910 --> 00:06:09,660
instead of asking me
to come here.

112
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:11,450
Yeah, not gonna happen.

113
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:14,670
Don't need Fuyuki's Blacklist
reciting all my personal info.

114
00:06:14,710 --> 00:06:16,130
Too risky.

115
00:06:16,170 --> 00:06:17,960
Go in there unarmed
and daemon-less?

116
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,130
You won't catch me
doin' that in a million years.

117
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:22,840
No one would attack you
if you were unarmed,

118
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,090
I assure you.

119
00:06:26,380 --> 00:06:28,180
[SHINGO]
Any other updates to share?

120
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:29,470
[ASUMA] No, none.

121
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:31,850
As I told you,
Asa stayed with us,

122
00:06:31,890 --> 00:06:33,430
and Yuru went with Tadera.

123
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:38,560
How could you let the Seal kid
walk out the door?

124
00:06:38,730 --> 00:06:39,820
Huh?

125
00:06:40,610 --> 00:06:41,650
Asuma...

126
00:06:42,150 --> 00:06:44,700
Quit wasting time
and make a move, boy.

127
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:47,570
You had a golden opportunity
to capture one of the twins,

128
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:48,780
and instead of seizing it,

129
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:50,620
you just sat on your ass
and watched.

130
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:52,040
Yuru may be young,

131
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:55,170
but he and his daemons
aren't easily beaten, Uncle.

132
00:06:55,210 --> 00:06:57,170
You would have
seen that for yourself

133
00:06:57,210 --> 00:06:58,670
if you had only been there.

134
00:06:58,710 --> 00:07:01,250
[Shingo grunting softly]

135
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,760
Get rid of that mangaka.

136
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:06,550
Make him disappear,
and the clan will be yours.

137
00:07:06,590 --> 00:07:09,470
Even if something
did happen to Hagure,

138
00:07:09,510 --> 00:07:11,060
I doubt the current head
of the clan

139
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,600
would conveniently drop dead.

140
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:16,230
If brute force isn't gonna work,
then win over Asa instead.

141
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:18,400
She's a naive little thing,
after all.

142
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:20,810
Just sweet talk her.
Make the girl yours.

143
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:23,940
I'm sure you know it's a crime
for an adult to make advances

144
00:07:23,990 --> 00:07:25,400
on a sixteen-year-old.

145
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:26,900
You some sort of square?

146
00:07:26,950 --> 00:07:31,030
[scoffs] I see you're every bit
as useless as your mother.

147
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,330
♪

148
00:07:33,490 --> 00:07:36,620
[ASUMA] Since I've nothing else
to report, I'll be going now.

149
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:38,210
I'll show myself out.

150
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:41,090
I meant what I said.

151
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:43,550
You should come
visit the manor sometime.

152
00:07:43,590 --> 00:07:45,210
-Give it a rest.
-[door opens]

153
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:46,550
[door closes]

154
00:07:47,590 --> 00:07:49,550
[toilet flushes]

155
00:07:52,890 --> 00:07:56,230
[IVAN] Oh. Did your nephew
leave already?

156
00:07:56,270 --> 00:07:57,480
Yeah.

157
00:07:57,520 --> 00:08:00,310
I forgot to tell him
that you had dropped by.

158
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:03,570
Whatever, I'm sure
you'll see him soon enough.

159
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:09,490
[Ivan sighs] I hate to say it.

160
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:12,120
Somebody ought to have
trained the boy better.

161
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:15,080
If you let your guard down
just because someone's family,

162
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:17,120
you're asking for trouble.

163
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:21,580
[keyboard clacking]

164
00:08:22,250 --> 00:08:24,750
[HANA] Taking care
of one kid is hard enough.

165
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,340
Two'll be even worse.

166
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,300
You sure this is a good idea?

167
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,510
It'll be fine, don't worry.

168
00:08:30,550 --> 00:08:33,390
That kid...
He's got his shit together.

169
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:37,310
Just look at what he did
after freeing Tenaga-Ashinaga.

170
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:39,310
He knew he had screwed up,

171
00:08:39,350 --> 00:08:42,150
and he was willing
to risk himself to fix it.

172
00:08:42,190 --> 00:08:43,770
-He's sharp, too.
-Oh! What is this?

173
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:45,230
[DERA] I bet he'll end up
being more of an asset

174
00:08:45,270 --> 00:08:47,240
-than you'd expect.
-A god of the wind held captive?

175
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:50,150
He's a good egg.
I can tell, you know.

176
00:08:50,990 --> 00:08:53,240
Yeah, well, trying hard
to be good all the time

177
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:55,530
can take a toll on a kid.
The effort of doing so

178
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:58,370
slowly starts wearing
their hearts out after a while.

179
00:08:58,410 --> 00:08:59,620
Uh? Jackpot.

180
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:01,040
I think this is it.

181
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,250
What is?

182
00:09:02,290 --> 00:09:04,880
A government database
of missing persons.

183
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,510
They've got a whole bunch
of info on here,

184
00:09:07,550 --> 00:09:08,590
like the last day

185
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:10,220
a missing person
was seen, you know?

186
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:12,470
So I've just been researching
and digging back

187
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:15,390
through the Tohoku records
from before Yuru was born.

188
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:17,470
Kinjo Nagisa.

189
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,560
[Yuru gasps]

190
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:20,100
[HANA]
Hiking registration form

191
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:22,730
found at the
Old Higashi Village Trailhead.

192
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:25,110
[DERA] The date
and age both match.

193
00:09:25,150 --> 00:09:28,360
It doesn't look like
her address is listed, though.

194
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:30,070
You mean my mom?

195
00:09:30,110 --> 00:09:32,950
Yeah, right? I'm thinking
that this must be her.

196
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:34,780
Back at the manor,

197
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:37,160
they told me that
my mom was from Okinawa.

198
00:09:37,830 --> 00:09:39,000
That would make sense.

199
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:41,620
Kinjo is a common name there.

200
00:09:41,910 --> 00:09:44,000
Here, this is how
you write Okinawa.

201
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:45,040
KINJO NAGISA
OKINAWA

202
00:09:45,290 --> 00:09:47,420
They said Nagisa vanished
while on a journey

203
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:49,260
to visit her parents,
did they not?

204
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:50,300
Yeah.

205
00:09:50,470 --> 00:09:52,880
[HANA] Which means we've got
a good idea

206
00:09:52,930 --> 00:09:54,760
of where your grandparents live.

207
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:57,220
[Yuru breathes uneasily]

208
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:59,430
[both grunting]
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

209
00:09:59,470 --> 00:10:01,140
I had Ryu Tadera tailed

210
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:03,310
and was able to locate
his hideout.

211
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:04,940
What did you do that for?

212
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,860
That's exactly the kind of move
we were avoiding.

213
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:10,070
We're attempting to earn
the brother's trust here.

214
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,530
They'll think
it was a clan decision,

215
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:13,990
and we'll be back to square one.

216
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:16,700
[ASUMA] As we thought,
it was a type of barrier.

217
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:18,660
One called a Lost House.

218
00:10:19,030 --> 00:10:21,200
One of the people
I sent returned,

219
00:10:21,250 --> 00:10:22,710
but two never will.

220
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:24,500
So they've gone missing
like the others?

221
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,040
No, they're dead.

222
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,790
We can be certain of that.

223
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:29,920
They were aged 19 and 40.

224
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,920
Both were single men
and neither of them

225
00:10:31,970 --> 00:10:34,130
had any friends
or family to speak of.

226
00:10:34,170 --> 00:10:35,260
[JIN] Hmm.

227
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:37,800
We can use their identities,

228
00:10:37,850 --> 00:10:39,680
so I'll leave them
as officially alive

229
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,270
in their family registers.

230
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:44,100
It's a shame, really.

231
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:46,690
If the 19-year-old
who died had been a woman,

232
00:10:46,730 --> 00:10:49,150
Gabby could have used
their identity.

233
00:10:50,730 --> 00:10:52,190
Her or Asa.

234
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:54,030
Deceased 16-year-old girls

235
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:57,280
without any close relations
are difficult to come by.

236
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:59,200
Let alone finding two of them.

237
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,910
Gabby seems to be fine

238
00:11:00,950 --> 00:11:03,080
with things the way
they are for now.

239
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:05,080
And Asa can be rather stubborn.

240
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:08,500
I doubt she would agree to claim
someone's identity as her own.

241
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:09,710
[phone ringing]

242
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:11,630
Yes. Hello?

243
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:13,800
[GABBY] You at the manor, Jinny?

244
00:11:15,050 --> 00:11:17,380
Asa got a call from someone.

245
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:19,800
Her gran in Okinawa.

246
00:11:19,850 --> 00:11:21,850
Oh, I'm doing great.

247
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:24,640
Yes. I'm so happy
that you've been well, too.

248
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:28,650
I promise, the Kagemoris
are taking good care of me.

249
00:11:28,690 --> 00:11:29,860
Yes.

250
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:33,320
No, I'm sorry.

251
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,570
I wish I could tell you,

252
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,570
but I still don't know
where Mom and Dad are.

253
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:38,820
[GRANDMA KINJO] I see.

254
00:11:39,030 --> 00:11:40,280
KINJO

255
00:11:40,330 --> 00:11:43,080
As long as it's been,
I keep expecting Nagisa

256
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:45,750
to turn up
out of the blue someday.

257
00:11:45,790 --> 00:11:47,210
Truth is,

258
00:11:47,410 --> 00:11:50,670
I'm getting old and the years
are starting to catch up to me.

259
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:53,550
And as much as I would love
to see Nagisa again,

260
00:11:54,210 --> 00:11:56,920
what I want more than anything
is to meet you.

261
00:11:56,970 --> 00:11:57,970
[Asa gasps]

262
00:11:58,470 --> 00:12:01,100
[GRANDMA KINJO] Please, dear,
you're my granddaughter.

263
00:12:01,140 --> 00:12:04,010
I'd like to see you once
before my health fails me

264
00:12:04,060 --> 00:12:05,390
and I lose the chance for good.

265
00:12:05,430 --> 00:12:07,690
[ASA] I'm really sorry, Grandma.

266
00:12:07,730 --> 00:12:09,770
I can't come visit you yet.

267
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:12,360
I would just cause trouble
for you.

268
00:12:13,770 --> 00:12:16,240
Yeah. I'm glad
I got to hear your voice.

269
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:18,860
Hope we'll chat again soon.
Love you.

270
00:12:22,990 --> 00:12:25,910
No change.
She was the same as always.

271
00:12:25,950 --> 00:12:27,080
[JIN] Hmm.

272
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:31,830
Every single word and phrase
was exactly the same.

273
00:12:32,590 --> 00:12:34,380
KINJO

274
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:37,470
I'd like to see you once
before my health fails me

275
00:12:37,510 --> 00:12:39,550
and I lose the chance for good.

276
00:12:39,590 --> 00:12:42,220
Please, dear,
you're my granddaughter.

277
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:45,260
I'd like to see you once
before my health fails me

278
00:12:45,310 --> 00:12:48,430
and I lose the chance for good.

279
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:53,730
I'd like to see you.

280
00:12:53,770 --> 00:12:56,570
I'd like to see you.

281
00:12:57,740 --> 00:12:59,990
[Asa inhales, sighs]

282
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:04,080
[Daifuku and Ohagi whine]

283
00:13:04,870 --> 00:13:06,870
[chuckles] Hey, it's okay.

284
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:08,870
I'm okay.

285
00:13:12,210 --> 00:13:13,290
[GABBY] Scumbags.

286
00:13:13,330 --> 00:13:14,880
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

287
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:18,800
So, next,
can we find these Kinjos

288
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,130
so that we can learn
about my mom?

289
00:13:20,170 --> 00:13:21,470
Do you have any idea

290
00:13:21,510 --> 00:13:23,840
how many Kinjos there are
in Okinawa?

291
00:13:23,890 --> 00:13:25,010
It's gotta be at least

292
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:26,890
the second most common surname
they've got.

293
00:13:26,930 --> 00:13:28,220
Think with me here.

294
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:30,810
Nagisa went missing while trying
to pay them a visit.

295
00:13:30,850 --> 00:13:33,100
We wouldn't want to draw
any more attention

296
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:34,650
to her family out there.

297
00:13:34,690 --> 00:13:36,320
They've been through a lot.

298
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:38,280
Don't need to put 'em
in danger, too.

299
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:39,490
[YURU] Hm.

300
00:13:39,570 --> 00:13:42,490
For all we know,
it's too late for old Kinjo.

301
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:44,240
And someone might
already be there

302
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:45,660
with a trap set for us.

303
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:48,830
The Kagemori family
offered to protect Nagisa.

304
00:13:48,870 --> 00:13:51,910
I'm sure they know which Kinjos
are the ones related to her.

305
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:53,830
With how secretive
the Kagemoris are,

306
00:13:53,870 --> 00:13:56,420
if they haven't taken that part
of the family under their wing,

307
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:58,550
well, it doesn't look good.

308
00:13:58,590 --> 00:13:59,800
[Yuru breathes uneasily]

309
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:01,550
[Dera sighs]

310
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:04,680
Guess the old Tadera clan head
is our best lead after all.

311
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:06,680
I'm gonna see the shaman.

312
00:14:07,390 --> 00:14:08,510
[KEN] Huh?

313
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:10,350
♪

314
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:29,240
PRAYERS - EXORCISMS
SPIRITUAL HEALING

315
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,950
Anyone in here?

316
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,410
Please, come on in!

317
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:35,920
How nice to get
an afternoon visit

318
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:37,170
from you like this!

319
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:39,420
I've got no more customers,
so close on up!

320
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:41,050
[DERA] I got it.

321
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,220
How was your village trip?

322
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:46,800
Like usual? Peaceful?

323
00:14:47,350 --> 00:14:50,100
[DERA] Yeah.
Actually, about that...

324
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:53,520
Little Azami from the village
will be turning seven soon.

325
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,810
So, it's time.

326
00:14:54,850 --> 00:14:55,890
[YAMA] Oh, yes.

327
00:14:56,230 --> 00:14:58,650
She's about ready to get her
vaccinations, isn't she?

328
00:14:58,690 --> 00:15:00,820
So, you just need
measles and rubella?

329
00:15:01,070 --> 00:15:02,570
I'll get them prepped for her.

330
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:06,030
Also, the village is a wreck
after a Kagemori attack.

331
00:15:06,070 --> 00:15:08,030
Talk about burying
the lead, there!

332
00:15:08,070 --> 00:15:09,620
Don't tack that on
like an afterthought

333
00:15:09,660 --> 00:15:10,990
to a kid's vaccination!

334
00:15:11,030 --> 00:15:12,540
That's why you're really here!

335
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:15,580
Gotta have your appetizer before
the main course is served.

336
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:17,040
[YAMA] Oh, I guess.

337
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:19,170
[DERA] So, let's talk.
I'm sure you've heard,

338
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:21,290
but one of the twins
is with the Kagemoris.

339
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:24,260
-[DERA] Hm? [chuckles]
-[YAMA] Yeah. They have Asa.

340
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:26,260
She acquired the power of Break

341
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,890
and used it to bust straight
through Higashi's barrier.

342
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:31,300
She brought
the Kagemoris with her.

343
00:15:31,350 --> 00:15:34,770
[gasps] What about Yuru?
They didn't take him, right?

344
00:15:34,810 --> 00:15:36,140
Calm down.

345
00:15:36,350 --> 00:15:38,270
I'm lookin' after
the kid myself.

346
00:15:38,310 --> 00:15:40,650
Granny told me
to take him and escape.

347
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:42,150
He's livin' down here.

348
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:44,070
[Yama groans softly]

349
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:47,240
We might've gotten
into a little scuffle

350
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:48,490
with some of the Kagemoris

351
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:50,070
as we were getting off
the mountain.

352
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,620
But we did eventually lose them.

353
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:54,040
Oh, please, no more!

354
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:56,870
We can't let another twin
fall into someone else's hands!

355
00:15:56,910 --> 00:15:58,120
Just no!

356
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:00,420
And you're sure it was
the power of Break?

357
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:01,590
[DERA] No doubt about it.

358
00:16:01,630 --> 00:16:04,000
Even said she got it
after she died once.

359
00:16:04,050 --> 00:16:05,000
[Yama chuckles]

360
00:16:05,050 --> 00:16:06,550
And here I was,

361
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:08,340
thinking Break and Seal
were nothing

362
00:16:08,380 --> 00:16:10,970
but the delusions
of the last generation!

363
00:16:11,350 --> 00:16:12,600
Well, anyway.

364
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:15,560
I'm not sure I can really
protect him by myself.

365
00:16:15,810 --> 00:16:18,600
I'd love a chance to pick
my predecessor's brain,

366
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:20,900
only I've got no clue
where he could be.

367
00:16:20,940 --> 00:16:23,320
You still haven't been able
to get in touch?

368
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:24,690
That must be hard for you.

369
00:16:24,730 --> 00:16:26,190
[DERA] It's been 10 years!

370
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:27,740
Haven't heard squat from him.

371
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:29,280
Any chance you have?

372
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:31,030
[YAMA] I'm afraid
I'm no better off

373
00:16:31,070 --> 00:16:32,620
than you are on that one.

374
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,990
I'm sure somebody'll
find him off

375
00:16:35,030 --> 00:16:36,160
in some ditch somewhere.

376
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:38,040
I could always ask around.

377
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:40,710
Want me to see if our
Higashi contacts have a lead?

378
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,670
[Dera sighs]
Please and thank you!

379
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:44,000
[YAMA] Hmm...

380
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:47,880
So, where are you hiding Yuru
now that he's in your care?

381
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:49,880
I got a secret second pad.

382
00:16:49,930 --> 00:16:51,850
♪

383
00:16:51,890 --> 00:16:53,680
Oh, good.

384
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:55,430
I'm sure he's safe there.

385
00:16:55,930 --> 00:16:57,220
[DERA] I don't know.

386
00:16:57,310 --> 00:16:59,940
I swear the kid's blood burns
hotter than the sun.

387
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:02,520
He knows how to talk a big game.

388
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:04,270
He said if anyone wants
his head,

389
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:05,570
they should come and get it.

390
00:17:05,610 --> 00:17:07,320
That after he beats them
black and blue,

391
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:09,360
he'll squeeze out their info.

392
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:12,370
[Yama sighs] Sounds like
he's looking for a fight!

393
00:17:12,410 --> 00:17:13,660
[DERA] Yeah, it sucks!

394
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:16,290
Wish he'd try putting himself
in my shoes!

395
00:17:16,330 --> 00:17:18,500
[chuckles] Anyway.

396
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:21,120
I've got my hands full
dealin' with that for a while,

397
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:23,920
so no chance I'll be able
to head up to the village.

398
00:17:24,250 --> 00:17:26,040
[YAMA] Oh, I get it.

399
00:17:26,090 --> 00:17:29,090
Well, maybe I'll check in
on the townsfolk

400
00:17:29,130 --> 00:17:31,130
while I'm there
for Azami's "exorcism."

401
00:17:31,170 --> 00:17:32,220
[DERA] Appreciate it.

402
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:34,220
Lot of folks are beaten up
real bad.

403
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:36,050
Make sure you bring
some medicine.

404
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:38,640
Oh, maybe that's why.

405
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:40,230
♪

406
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:44,650
[YAMA] Last night,
I was accosted by a strange man!

407
00:17:46,650 --> 00:17:48,110
He had some katanas.

408
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:51,570
Well, considering there were
two of them,

409
00:17:51,610 --> 00:17:53,150
they must've been daemons.

410
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,370
Probably.

411
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:57,330
And in a flash,
he closed the distance.

412
00:17:57,370 --> 00:17:58,490
[Yama and Tsugais yell]

413
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:01,790
[Tsugais squealing]

414
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:04,330
-[DERA] Did he cut you?
-[YAMA] No.

415
00:18:05,330 --> 00:18:08,000
When I came to,
I was lying in the street.

416
00:18:08,050 --> 00:18:10,590
I didn't have a scratch on me.

417
00:18:12,470 --> 00:18:15,220
At the time, I thought he was
some pervert.

418
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:16,300
Still could be!

419
00:18:16,350 --> 00:18:18,470
But now, I have my doubts.

420
00:18:18,510 --> 00:18:20,430
I wonder if he was after Yuru.

421
00:18:20,470 --> 00:18:22,520
So, a pair of katanas.

422
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:24,640
Hmm. I'll keep an eye out.

423
00:18:25,810 --> 00:18:28,270
If you do find out
something about my predecessor,

424
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:30,900
-I wanna be the first to know.
-Sure thing!

425
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:36,410
And don't get tailed
into the village, Mr. Shaman.

426
00:18:36,450 --> 00:18:37,490
Be careful.

427
00:18:37,530 --> 00:18:39,200
[scoffs] No need to worry.

428
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:41,080
-I always am.
-[door closes]

429
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:44,750
[bird cawing]

430
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:47,330
[YAMA] Oh, dear!

431
00:18:47,840 --> 00:18:51,420
No, no, no.
This is simply terrible!

432
00:18:54,010 --> 00:18:57,100
Signs of mourning
everywhere you look.

433
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,260
-[BOY 1] It's the shaman!
-[Yama gasps]

434
00:19:00,310 --> 00:19:01,390
[BOY 2] Mr. Yama!

435
00:19:01,430 --> 00:19:03,520
[YAMA] Oh, my darling munchkins!

436
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:05,230
You're all all right!

437
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:06,730
[BOY 1] It was awful!

438
00:19:07,310 --> 00:19:10,190
Some strangers came
and killed people, Mr. Yama!

439
00:19:10,230 --> 00:19:12,400
Dera already let me know.

440
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,610
They had iron birds

441
00:19:13,650 --> 00:19:15,650
and iron shooty-ball things,
too!

442
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:18,160
It was so scary. And loud!

443
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,450
And look way over there!

444
00:19:19,490 --> 00:19:21,290
Left and Right are gone!

445
00:19:21,330 --> 00:19:24,410
[BOY 2] I think an evil god
must've come to the village!

446
00:19:24,450 --> 00:19:25,870
What's happening?

447
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:27,420
Are Left and Right broken?

448
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:29,750
The strangers had
some invisible power.

449
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:32,670
They were cutting a bunch
of grown-ups in half so easily.

450
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,130
[YAMA] Hmm...

451
00:19:34,170 --> 00:19:36,760
They killed Azami's Ma
in front of her.

452
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:39,890
'Kay...

453
00:19:39,930 --> 00:19:41,890
Get ready
to feel the god!

454
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:45,020
Hold still.
There might be a little pinch.

455
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:49,060
There! Finished!

456
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:52,530
You're now protected
from the evil gods of sickness.

457
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:57,530
All done, Azami.
You're free to go.

458
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:01,490
[Azami groans softly]

459
00:20:03,950 --> 00:20:06,250
[gasps, sighs]

460
00:20:15,630 --> 00:20:18,800
[MAN 1] Poor kid.
Watched her mother get beheaded.

461
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:21,720
Damn Kagemoris will pay
for what they did to us.

462
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:24,310
Mr. Yama, are you safe?

463
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:27,100
You weren't shadowed
by the Kagemoris, were you?

464
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:30,650
[YAMA] No. Someone was trying
near the base of the mountain,

465
00:20:30,690 --> 00:20:31,730
but I shook them.

466
00:20:31,860 --> 00:20:34,030
Goes to show
we should've been proactive.

467
00:20:34,110 --> 00:20:35,780
If we already had
our hands on Seal,

468
00:20:35,820 --> 00:20:36,940
this would've gone different.

469
00:20:36,990 --> 00:20:38,700
It's just one boy's life.

470
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:41,070
It wasn't worth letting
the Kagemoris roll over us.

471
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:42,450
-[YAMA] Five bandits.
-[all gasp]

472
00:20:42,490 --> 00:20:44,200
You think we haven't tried?

473
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:47,080
We sent five of our
most elite bandits after him,

474
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:49,210
and all of them wound up
with an arrow in the neck

475
00:20:49,250 --> 00:20:50,920
or a blade in their ribs.

476
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:52,750
He's skilled enough
to shoot a pheasant

477
00:20:52,790 --> 00:20:54,170
straight out of the air.

478
00:20:54,210 --> 00:20:57,090
A human may
as well be a snail.

479
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:59,550
You lot wouldn't have stood
a chance against him.

480
00:20:59,590 --> 00:21:00,630
[all sigh]

481
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:03,300
At minimum,
you'd need to take a hostage

482
00:21:03,350 --> 00:21:05,010
so you'd have something on him.

483
00:21:05,060 --> 00:21:06,350
[IVAN] Good idea.

484
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:08,100
-[slashing]
-[TSUGAIS] Uh?

485
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:09,230
[YAMA] Uh?

486
00:21:09,890 --> 00:21:11,480
What?

487
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:13,060
[both gasp]

488
00:21:13,110 --> 00:21:15,650
[Yama screams]

489
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:24,740
Higashi Village!
Good to see you!

490
00:21:24,780 --> 00:21:27,080
[Yama yells]

491
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,660
What's going on with my body?

492
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:33,380
[gasps] I know you!
You're that pervert!

493
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:34,750
That's so rude.

494
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:39,550
I'm Ivan Yosano,
not some common pervert.

495
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:42,180
-What's happening?
-Is he holding something?

496
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:46,180
Oh, you can't see
my daemons, can you?

497
00:21:48,560 --> 00:21:50,180
[men groaning]

498
00:21:51,020 --> 00:21:54,440
[IVAN] Great.
That makes my job easy.

499
00:21:55,150 --> 00:21:57,400
[♪ closing theme song playing]

500
00:23:26,450 --> 00:23:27,740
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

501
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:31,040
[IVAN] Look at you.
You look like Asa.

502
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:32,330
[SHINGO] Ivan, you're up.

503
00:23:32,410 --> 00:23:34,660
[OSHIRASAMA] Shall we stop
by the rest area?

504
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:37,750
[KYOKA] Yuru needs you,
so get outta here.

505
00:23:37,790 --> 00:23:39,840
EPISODE 13
DAIKYO AND SHOKYO
